6,Eastern Kayah - eky (Sino-Tibetan) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/eky/,"Eastern Kayah (eky) is part of the Sino-Tibetan family and Sino-Tibetan, Tibeto-Burman, Karenic, Central class. Eastern Kayah speaking People Groups across the world: Fast Facts","Kayah, Eastern",Sino-Tibetan
7,WALS Online - Language Kayah Li (Eastern),https://wals.info/languoid/lect/wals_code_kyl,Language Kayah Li (Eastern). WALS code: kyl.Glottocode: east2342. ISO 639-3: eky.,"Kayah, Eastern",Sino-Tibetan
8,"Full text of ""Eastern Kayah Li: Grammar, Texts, Glossary""",https://archive.org/stream/rosettaproject_kyu_detail-1/rosettaproject_kyu_detail-1_djvu.txt,"0,1 Kayah, Karen, Karenni. 0.1.1 General Remarks. The language described in this study is an Eastern dialect of Kayah Li. Kayah in turn is a Central Karen language, and Karen is a major subdivision of the Tibeto-Burman branch of Sino-Tibetan.","Kayah, Eastern",Sino-Tibetan
